==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|deyja|lang=non}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈteiːja/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|eiːja|lang=is}}
*: Homophones: {{l|is|deigja}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|dó|dóu|dáið}}
# {{intransitive|lang=is}} to [[die]]{{jump|is|die|s}}
#: ''Hún '''dó''' úr krabbameini.''
#:: She '''died''' of cancer.
#: ''Hundruð manna '''dóu''' úr hor.''
#:: Hundreds '''died''' of hunger.
#: ''Við munum öll '''deyja'''!''
#:: We are all going to '''die'''!
#: ''Að '''deyja''' úr kulda.''
#:: To '''die''' from exposure.
# {{intransitive|lang=is}} to [[pass out]] from drinking
# {{intransitive|of fire|lang=is}} to [[go out]]{{jump|is|of fire, go out|s}}
# {{intransitive|nautical|of the ocean|lang=is}} to [[calm down]], to [[subside]]
# {{intransitive|of grass|lang=is}} to [[wither]]

====Derived terms====
* [[deyja af]], [[deyja niður]], [[deyja út]] (''of weather or sea'' to calm down)
* [[deyja burt]] (''archaic'' to die)
* [[deyja drottni sínum]]
* [[deyja fyrir hendi|deyja fyrir hendi einhver]] (to die at the hands of someone)
* [[deyja ekki ráðalaus]] (to not to give up easily)
* [[deyja niður]] (to die in heaps)
* [[deyja úr hor]], [[deyja úr hungri]] (to starve to death, to die of starvation, to die of hunger)
* [[deyja út]] (to become extinct, to die out)
* [[deyja út af]] (to die a natural death, ''confer'' [[lognast út af]])
* [[deyja úti]] (''of hay'' not make it to the barn, left out in times of autumn)

====Related terms====
* [[dauði]]
* [[dauður]]
* [[dá]]

